    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nouméa</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVitty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nouméa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-22T10:00:00+11:00">October 22,
                            1941—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Department’s 16, October 15, 7 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d565-f1"/> The
                    situation with regard to landing bases here is: three land bases are under
                    construction, one nearing completion and the other two being cleared for
                    emergency landing fields. These bases are being constructed by the local
                    government for Australia with materials furnished by that Government. All these
                    bases can be greatly improved and it is my opinion that the War Department’s
                    needs would be best served by cooperating with the Australian Government in the
                    improvement of the projects already under way here; in view of this I am not
                    taking the matter up with the High Commissioner upon his arrival here, pending
                    further instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d565-f1" n="7" xml:id="d565-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram repeated telegram No. 4458, October 15, 7 p.m., to the Ambassador
                    in the United Kingdom, <ref target="#pg573">p. 573</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
